From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lierfang Support Team <itsupport@lierfang.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 00:03:16 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] target/loongarch/kvm: resolve msgint=auto after the KVM
 feature check

With "-cpu max" msgint defaults to auto. kvm_cpu_check_msgint() clears
CPUCFG1.MSG_INT when KVM lacks the msgint feature, but leaves the property
at auto. virt_check_dmsi() runs after the vCPUs are realized and only
looks at the property, so it still enables DMSI: the DINTC device is
created and the guest is told through the IOCSR misc feature register
that direct message interrupts are available. The guest then configures
its interrupts for DMSI and hangs at boot (black screen) on hosts without
KVM msgint support, e.g. openEuler kernels before 6.6.0-19.

Resolve auto to on/off in kvm_cpu_check_msgint(), like the PMU check does,
so the virt machine sees the effective state.
---
 target/loongarch/kvm/kvm.c | 14 ++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/target/loongarch/kvm/kvm.c b/target/loongarch/kvm/kvm.c
index 0ff7433fda..6792363d21 100644
--- a/target/loongarch/kvm/kvm.c
+++ b/target/loongarch/kvm/kvm.c
@@ -1222,8 +1222,18 @@ static int kvm_cpu_check_msgint(CPUState *cs, Error **errp)
             error_setg(errp, "'msgint' feature not supported by KVM on this host");
             return -ENOTSUP;
         }
-    } else if ((cpu->msgint == ON_OFF_AUTO_AUTO) && kvm_supported) {
-        env->cpucfg[1] = FIELD_DP32(env->cpucfg[1], CPUCFG1, MSG_INT, 1);
+    } else if (cpu->msgint == ON_OFF_AUTO_AUTO) {
+        /*
+         * Resolve "auto" so that the virt machine, which checks the
+         * property after the vCPUs are realized, does not enable DMSI
+         * on a host without KVM msgint support.
+         */
+        if (kvm_supported) {
+            env->cpucfg[1] = FIELD_DP32(env->cpucfg[1], CPUCFG1, MSG_INT, 1);
+            cpu->msgint = ON_OFF_AUTO_ON;
+        } else {
+            cpu->msgint = ON_OFF_AUTO_OFF;
+        }
     }
 
     return 0;
